1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:03,067
<i>Didn't you say to call you
when I found a USB?</i>

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:05,900
<i>There's someone here,
a message for Andrew.</i>

3
00:00:06,033 --> 00:00:08,633
<i> I know who got it, it's Panot!</i>

4
00:00:08,767 --> 00:00:10,500
<i>He said someone wanted
to buy it.</i>

5
00:00:10,633 --> 00:00:11,667
<i> Well then, I'll buy it.</i>

6
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:13,300
<i>Be careful when you go to Panot.</i>

7
00:00:13,433 --> 00:00:14,867
<i>The woman at the market
is here again.</i>

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:15,867
<i>It looks like she's looking
for something.</i>

9
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,567
<i> Hurry up! Go there!</i>

10
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:18,400
<i> Okay, Madam.</i>

11
00:00:18,533 --> 00:00:19,933
<i> Where can I find that Panot?</i>

12
00:00:20,067 --> 00:00:22,067
<i>This is the factory they're
talking about in Purok Tres.</i>

13
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:24,400
<i>You still can't find the woman?</i>

14
00:00:24,533 --> 00:00:27,200
<i>But we have an update, Madam.
There's an addict at the market.</i>

15
00:00:27,333 --> 00:00:28,867
<i> He's selling a USB</i>

16
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,333
<i>with a video of the deceased
Police Officer Bolagos.</i>

17
00:00:31,467 --> 00:00:33,500
<i> I'll deal with them myself.</i>

18
00:00:33,633 --> 00:00:35,533
<i>Miguel, is there anyone outside
helping you?</i>

19
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:37,933
<i> I'll tell you when I'm sure.</i>

20
00:00:38,067 --> 00:00:39,767
<i>Don't you trust me anymore,
Buddy?</i>

21
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:42,100
<i>They're buying the USB
from the gang of addicts.</i>

22
00:00:42,233 --> 00:00:44,533
<i>Give me the flash drive.
You don't want it.</i>

23
00:00:44,667 --> 00:00:45,600
<i> Gotcha!</i>

24
00:00:45,733 --> 00:00:47,033
<i> You guys are crazy!</i>

25
00:00:47,167 --> 00:00:48,867
<i> The deal earlier was clear?</i>

26
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:50,633
<i>- Give it to me.
- Damn you!</i>

27
00:00:50,767 --> 00:00:54,000
<i>It's time to meet that freakin'
girl and get that video.</i>

28
00:01:16,267 --> 00:01:17,100
What's that?

29
00:01:17,233 --> 00:01:19,167
You even brought a backup!

30
00:01:27,233 --> 00:01:28,367
The video...

31
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,600
I found you, Theresa Park.

32
00:01:55,833 --> 00:01:57,033
Joey, let's go!

33
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,133
The flash drive.

34
00:02:03,267 --> 00:02:04,533
No, don't.

35
00:02:07,333 --> 00:02:08,500
Joey, don't!

36
00:02:10,533 --> 00:02:11,433
Joey!

37
00:02:26,667 --> 00:02:28,100
So it's you.

38
00:02:28,233 --> 00:02:30,367
Well, I wanted to meet you.

39
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:32,433
But this will do.

40
00:02:48,067 --> 00:02:50,367
Joey, this way!

41
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:51,800
Madam, you are hit.

42
00:02:51,933 --> 00:02:54,067
Come on, let's get Madam
out of here!

43
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:55,433
Let's go.

44
00:02:56,567 --> 00:02:58,033
Get down! Get down!

45
00:03:20,067 --> 00:03:20,733
Hey!

46
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:22,800
You?

47
00:03:22,933 --> 00:03:25,000
What are you doing here?

48
00:03:25,133 --> 00:03:25,933
Do you know him?

49
00:03:26,067 --> 00:03:26,867
No.

50
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,600
Now is not the time for talking.

51
00:03:28,733 --> 00:03:30,833
Just stay here, okay?

52
00:03:30,967 --> 00:03:31,700
You...

53
00:03:31,833 --> 00:03:33,333
Can you protect them?

54
00:03:33,467 --> 00:03:34,533
I got to go.

55
00:03:34,667 --> 00:03:36,933
Wait! Just don't leave!
Come back...

56
00:03:43,067 --> 00:03:44,433
Stop!

57
00:03:46,867 --> 00:03:47,833
Jin Ho?

58
00:03:50,333 --> 00:03:52,333
I got you now.

59
00:03:52,467 --> 00:03:54,433
What are you waiting for?
Shoot him!

60
00:04:17,833 --> 00:04:18,900
No more shooting.

61
00:04:20,067 --> 00:04:21,667
Maybe they're all dead.

62
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:24,200
That's why let's leave now.

63
00:04:52,167 --> 00:04:53,467
Get in the car.

64
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:54,633
Why?

65
00:04:54,767 --> 00:04:56,667
You're not out of danger.

66
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:59,167
They might stay around
to follow you.

67
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:00,900
You can't go home now.

68
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,400
My car is also far away.

69
00:05:05,433 --> 00:05:07,733
If they catch us on a motorbike,
we don't stand a chance either.

70
00:05:07,867 --> 00:05:10,767
You want them to find you here,
or are we going?

71
00:05:14,967 --> 00:05:16,133
Let's go.

72
00:05:16,267 --> 00:05:17,367
Let's go.

73
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:31,333
Beauty!

74
00:05:34,100 --> 00:05:35,400
Come in.

75
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:47,167
So...

76
00:05:48,467 --> 00:05:49,800
You're safe here.

77
00:05:50,833 --> 00:05:51,733
Who are you really,

78
00:05:51,867 --> 00:05:53,667
and why are you always
showing up?

79
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:55,267
I'm sorry.

80
00:05:55,400 --> 00:05:56,600
I'm sorry?

81
00:05:56,733 --> 00:05:59,167
You should learn our language.
You're in our country.

82
00:05:59,300 --> 00:06:00,767
And not that I'm the one
who gets nosebleeds

83
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:02,500
because of you before
we understand each other.

84
00:06:04,067 --> 00:06:05,967
How did you meet him?

85
00:06:06,100 --> 00:06:07,667
That's my stalker.

86
00:06:07,833 --> 00:06:10,233
He's the one who saved me
at the market.

87
00:06:10,367 --> 00:06:11,433
Stalker?

88
00:06:11,567 --> 00:06:16,667
Hey, I'm your savior.
I saved your life twice!

89
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:21,367
But why are you always near her
when she gets in trouble?

90
00:06:21,500 --> 00:06:22,600
Because he's a stalker.

91
00:06:22,733 --> 00:06:23,900
Hey!

92
00:06:24,033 --> 00:06:27,633
No need for violence, okay.
I'll explain everything.

93
00:06:27,767 --> 00:06:28,533
And no...

94
00:06:28,667 --> 00:06:31,267
No pepper spray,

95
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:32,200
please.

96
00:06:43,067 --> 00:06:45,367
Calm down, okay?

97
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:50,333
So my name is Jin Ho,
Lee Jin Ho.

98
00:06:50,467 --> 00:06:53,967
I am from the National
Intelligence Service in Korea.

99
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:54,933
Yes,

100
00:06:55,067 --> 00:06:56,333
I'm an agent.

101
00:07:03,833 --> 00:07:05,333
So,

102
00:07:05,467 --> 00:07:08,933
I'm looking for a crime boss
from Korea.

103
00:07:11,567 --> 00:07:16,900
And I need to bring her back
to our country.

104
00:07:17,067 --> 00:07:21,000
Recently, she's hiding here
in the Philippines.

105
00:07:21,133 --> 00:07:24,167
She changed her name,
even her face.

106
00:07:24,300 --> 00:07:26,033
Why are you following me?

107
00:07:26,167 --> 00:07:28,067
Do I look like a crime boss
to you?

108
00:07:28,200 --> 00:07:29,467
I'm just a student.

109
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:31,233
The woman in the video.

110
00:07:32,567 --> 00:07:35,667
The one you posted
on the internet.

111
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:38,333
It's Theresa Park.

112
00:07:38,467 --> 00:07:40,533
That's the one I'm looking for.

113
00:07:45,067 --> 00:07:47,100
You're lucky it's just
a graze wound.

114
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:53,833
That was supposed
to be an easy job!

115
00:07:53,967 --> 00:07:56,767
I was about to kill that...

116
00:07:56,900 --> 00:08:01,100
but then Jin ho ruined
everything!

117
00:08:01,233 --> 00:08:03,967
You'll be in trouble when
Berdugo finds out about this.

118
00:08:04,100 --> 00:08:06,667
Loloy can now clean the site.

119
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:08,800
That's the least of my concerns.

120
00:08:08,933 --> 00:08:13,600
My problem now, aside from that
freakin' video, is Jin Ho!

121
00:08:13,733 --> 00:08:15,900
He found me!

122
00:08:16,033 --> 00:08:17,533
<i> Stop!</i>

123
00:08:17,667 --> 00:08:18,533
<i> Jin ho?</i>

124
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,467
<i> I got you now.</i>

125
00:08:21,633 --> 00:08:24,633
He recognized me! He saw me!

126
00:08:24,767 --> 00:08:27,700
That Jin Ho won't stop
bothering me!

127
00:08:27,833 --> 00:08:30,067
This is how I found you.

128
00:08:31,533 --> 00:08:35,367
You posted the video using
an anonymous account,

129
00:08:35,500 --> 00:08:37,467
but it's not that hard to track.

130
00:08:38,933 --> 00:08:42,967
So this Theresa Park
that you're talking about

131
00:08:43,100 --> 00:08:47,000
is an international crime boss?

132
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:50,833
What's her business?

133
00:08:52,367 --> 00:08:53,333
Drugs?

134
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:56,400
Yes.

135
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,000
That Theresa Park,

136
00:08:59,133 --> 00:09:02,033
that's the one who killed
Ramon Orbos, not Father.

137
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:05,033
We already have proof now.

138
00:09:06,467 --> 00:09:08,567
How can we help Father?

139
00:09:08,700 --> 00:09:10,633
Let's go. Let's check the stuff
in the shop.

140
00:09:10,767 --> 00:09:11,667
Hey, stop!

141
00:09:14,100 --> 00:09:16,100
You're not going anywhere.

142
00:09:17,400 --> 00:09:18,400
What?

143
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:40,567
<i> To be honest,</i>

144
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:43,767
<i>I don't know the person
I married anymore.</i>

145
00:09:43,900 --> 00:09:47,033
<i>Well, then, don't come back
here.</i>

146
00:09:47,167 --> 00:09:48,833
<i> I don't need your pity.</i>

147
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:06,200
It's Mother.

148
00:10:06,333 --> 00:10:07,500
No phone.

149
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:22,567
Clarissa.

150
00:10:22,700 --> 00:10:24,733
I thought you left already.

151
00:10:24,867 --> 00:10:26,700
I can't leave you alone.

152
00:10:26,833 --> 00:10:28,600
I'm worried about you.

153
00:10:28,733 --> 00:10:32,233
I brought you some food.
Have you eaten yet?

154
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,400
Why do you seem worried?
Is there a problem, Clarissa?

155
00:10:36,533 --> 00:10:38,100
Why?

156
00:10:38,233 --> 00:10:40,967
Joey isn't answering my calls.

157
00:10:42,067 --> 00:10:43,133
What's with you?

158
00:10:44,433 --> 00:10:45,633
Give me my phone.

159
00:10:45,767 --> 00:10:47,667
Give me my phone!

160
00:10:47,800 --> 00:10:49,400
Give me that back!

161
00:10:52,300 --> 00:10:53,100
Ouch!

162
00:10:59,633 --> 00:11:01,467
Ouch!

163
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:04,100
Won't you help?
Don't you have a gun?

164
00:11:04,233 --> 00:11:07,833
Joey, let's listen to him first.

165
00:11:08,967 --> 00:11:12,133
Aren't you curious
about what he is saying?

166
00:11:12,267 --> 00:11:15,667
What if it's connected
to your father's case?

167
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:17,067
What are you saying?

168
00:11:24,633 --> 00:11:25,500
Fine!

169
00:11:25,633 --> 00:11:27,433
Let Peter go first,
then I'll listen to you!

170
00:11:27,567 --> 00:11:28,900
We have to feel safe first!

171
00:11:32,667 --> 00:11:33,633
Listen.

172
00:11:33,767 --> 00:11:36,767
This is the safest place
for you now.

173
00:11:36,900 --> 00:11:39,600
If you leave,
those men will come after you.

174
00:11:39,733 --> 00:11:42,100
They will follow you
to your house, to your family...

175
00:11:43,267 --> 00:11:44,867
And they will kill you.

176
00:11:46,967 --> 00:11:50,633
So please stay here
until I get Theresa.

177
00:11:52,067 --> 00:11:55,233
Then you'll be safe.
I'll make sure of it.

178
00:11:55,367 --> 00:11:56,300
I promise.

179
00:12:03,567 --> 00:12:04,267
Fine.

180
00:12:05,367 --> 00:12:06,533
We will stay.

181
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:09,133
What?

182
00:12:11,367 --> 00:12:13,167
Joey, he's right.

183
00:12:13,300 --> 00:12:15,833
After what happened to us
earlier,

184
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:22,700
we're not sure if Theresa is
following us or waiting for us.

185
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:28,800
So yeah,

186
00:12:28,933 --> 00:12:33,733
we'll be staying here for the
night since we're all exhausted.

187
00:12:33,867 --> 00:12:38,000
But tomorrow, we'll figure out
what to do with Theresa.

188
00:12:39,133 --> 00:12:41,133
Maybe the kid is just busy.

189
00:12:42,867 --> 00:12:45,567
I'm nervous too, Diego.

190
00:12:47,333 --> 00:12:48,333
Wait.

191
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:56,167
What?

192
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:01,967
Okay, we'll stay.

193
00:13:02,100 --> 00:13:03,900
I just need to talk
to my Mother first.

194
00:13:08,833 --> 00:13:11,867
Do not tell her your situation.

195
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:16,567
This remains confidential
until it's over.

196
00:13:22,333 --> 00:13:23,567
Hello, Mother?

197
00:13:23,700 --> 00:13:27,067
Joey, why aren't you answering
your phone?

198
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:28,400
Are you still out?

199
00:13:28,533 --> 00:13:30,100
<i> What time is it?</i>

200
00:13:31,467 --> 00:13:33,633
I'm just at the boarding house.

201
00:13:33,767 --> 00:13:38,000
I've got a lot of work
to do with my project.

202
00:13:38,133 --> 00:13:40,300
<i> Have you visited Father yet?</i>

203
00:13:43,467 --> 00:13:45,800
Your Godfather Diego
went to see him.

204
00:13:45,933 --> 00:13:48,400
<i> He said your father is okay.</i>

205
00:13:49,567 --> 00:13:52,567
<i>Joey, your mother is worried
about you.</i>

206
00:13:52,700 --> 00:13:55,067
How are you? Are you okay?

207
00:13:55,233 --> 00:13:56,633
Godfather...

208
00:14:01,367 --> 00:14:02,500
Finish it.

209
00:14:04,633 --> 00:14:06,833
Godfather, okay, next time,
okay?

210
00:14:06,967 --> 00:14:09,233
I still have a lot to do.

211
00:14:09,367 --> 00:14:11,633
Mother, I love you.

212
00:14:11,767 --> 00:14:13,867
Love you, Joey! Call me, okay?

213
00:14:18,667 --> 00:14:19,633
Happy?

214
00:14:20,967 --> 00:14:22,767
You don't have to be mad at me.

215
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:25,067
I'm doing this for your sake.

216
00:14:27,067 --> 00:14:28,467
Okay.

217
00:14:28,633 --> 00:14:30,567
We are all tired.

218
00:14:31,767 --> 00:14:33,433
Let's just rest.

219
00:14:50,067 --> 00:14:52,300
So, you can have this room.

220
00:14:52,433 --> 00:14:53,967
I'll sleep on the couch.

221
00:14:54,100 --> 00:14:57,567
What? So you can watch over us?
So we can't escape, right?

222
00:14:57,700 --> 00:15:00,767
Maybe you want to take
our cell phones.

223
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:03,633
Yes, give me your cell phones.

224
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:05,767
No way!

225
00:15:07,467 --> 00:15:08,667
Give it to him.

226
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:13,367
Can't you be apart from your
cell phones for even one night?

227
00:15:14,967 --> 00:15:16,000
Go ahead.

228
00:15:17,300 --> 00:15:18,633
Give me.

229
00:15:18,767 --> 00:15:19,867
Phone.

230
00:15:29,500 --> 00:15:30,467
You.

231
00:15:36,133 --> 00:15:38,033
So everybody, listen.

232
00:15:38,167 --> 00:15:41,233
You can't call anyone tonight.

233
00:15:41,367 --> 00:15:43,200
Don't worry.
I keep the big ones.

234
00:15:43,333 --> 00:15:45,200
I can't trust all of you.

235
00:15:45,333 --> 00:15:48,067
But with you, we can trust you,
is that it?

236
00:15:49,867 --> 00:15:50,900
Your gun.

237
00:15:54,733 --> 00:15:55,767
My gun?

238
00:15:55,900 --> 00:15:56,900
Yes.

239
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:05,900
Here.

240
00:16:09,100 --> 00:16:12,233
I'll bring you what you need.
Just wait for me.

241
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:19,333
Andrew!

242
00:16:19,467 --> 00:16:20,733
Why did you give him your gun?

243
00:16:20,867 --> 00:16:23,667
Now we don't stand a chance
against him.

244
00:16:23,800 --> 00:16:26,467
Joey, if he wanted to kill us,

245
00:16:26,600 --> 00:16:29,100
he would have done it
a while ago.

246
00:16:29,233 --> 00:16:31,700
And you said he saved you twice.

247
00:16:31,833 --> 00:16:35,133
So you two, stop complaining
so much.

248
00:16:35,267 --> 00:16:37,033
You're whining a lot.

249
00:16:43,900 --> 00:16:46,367
I really don't trust
that Andrew.

250
00:16:47,367 --> 00:16:50,700
I think he wouldn't sleep in
someone's house, would he?

251
00:16:50,833 --> 00:16:52,367
You know, let him go.

252
00:16:52,500 --> 00:16:54,500
Just get some rest.

253
00:16:54,633 --> 00:16:56,167
I won't sleep.

254
00:16:56,300 --> 00:16:57,467
I'll watch over you.

255
00:20:40,767 --> 00:20:41,633
Hey.

256
00:20:43,967 --> 00:20:45,900
What are you doing there?

257
00:20:46,033 --> 00:20:47,267
Why are you here?

258
00:20:47,400 --> 00:20:49,067
Isn't it time for you to go
to bed?

259
00:20:49,200 --> 00:20:51,000
I knew it.

260
00:20:51,133 --> 00:20:54,633
I knew it! You're just lying
about trusting Jin Ho.

261
00:20:57,367 --> 00:20:58,933
What are you looking for there?

262
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:03,433
Can't you just not talk?

263
00:21:03,567 --> 00:21:05,800
You're the one who got us
involved here.

264
00:21:05,933 --> 00:21:07,700
That's why you don't want us
to leave

265
00:21:07,833 --> 00:21:09,967
because you want to include this
in your story too.

266
00:21:10,967 --> 00:21:12,267
What if something happens
to Peter and me?

267
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:13,800
Is there anything you can do?

268
00:21:15,400 --> 00:21:16,833
Just don't make a noise.

269
00:21:16,967 --> 00:21:18,467
What are you doing there?

270
00:21:21,400 --> 00:21:23,000
What are you doing?

271
00:21:29,700 --> 00:21:30,733
Get up.

272
00:21:37,633 --> 00:21:40,433
Step away from my things.

273
00:21:43,967 --> 00:21:46,033
Please don't kill us.
It's his fault!

274
00:21:46,167 --> 00:21:47,100
Yes.

275
00:21:47,233 --> 00:21:48,467
Well, she's right.

276
00:21:50,200 --> 00:21:52,233
Keep her out of this.

277
00:21:53,400 --> 00:21:56,933
This is between you and me.

278
00:22:26,933 --> 00:22:28,500
So you want us to stay

279
00:22:28,633 --> 00:22:30,800
because you want to put your
story on your vlog.

280
00:22:30,933 --> 00:22:32,333
Isn't that what you did
to my Father?

281
00:22:32,467 --> 00:22:33,633
And now, you're going to do it
to us?

282
00:22:33,767 --> 00:22:36,233
You're good at getting other
people into trouble.

283
00:22:36,367 --> 00:22:37,900
Can you fix the flash drive?

284
00:22:38,033 --> 00:22:40,967
Did you ask your people
if they saw the flash drive?

285
00:22:41,100 --> 00:22:43,300
It contains a video
of Ramon and me.

286
00:22:43,433 --> 00:22:44,967
Godfather, can we meet?

287
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:48,533
About the evidence I'm saying
will help Father.

288
00:22:48,700 --> 00:22:51,133
You're still in danger.
I'm here to protect you.

289
00:22:51,267 --> 00:22:53,567
Maybe that policeman can still
perform a miracle.

290
00:22:53,700 --> 00:22:55,133
Why don't we just kill him?

291
00:22:55,267 --> 00:22:57,367
I think that Parak holds
a position.

292
00:22:57,500 --> 00:22:58,367
This is it!

293
00:22:58,500 --> 00:23:00,067
Joey, I'd like to introduce you
to someone!

294
00:23:00,200 --> 00:23:00,733
You?

295
00:23:00,867 --> 00:23:04,467
His name is Jin Ho!
